
Technical Design Document: Configurable Rule Engine
1. System Overview & Architecture
The objective of this design is to provide a scalable, database-driven Rule Engine in Java. Instead of hardcoding business rules in Java code, rules are modeled as configurable records in Oracle DB.

The engine evaluates incoming assessment answers—represented as Map<String, List<String>> (where the key is a QuestionId and the value is a list of selected answers)—and evaluates them against atomic conditions grouped into logical rules.

       +-----------------------+
       |   Incoming Payload    |
       | Map<String, List<S>>  |
       +-----------+-----------+
                   |
                   v
       +-----------------------+
       |   Rule Engine Logic   | <---> [ Cached Rules Metadata ]
       +-----------+-----------+
                   |
                   v
       +-----------------------+
       | Calculated Outcome    |
       |  (Disposition Types)  |
       +-----------------------+
2. Oracle Database Design
To ensure performance and scalability, rules are split into three normalized tables:

RULE_DISPOSITION: Defines the target outcome/disposition.

BUSINESS_RULE: Defines an individual rule under a disposition. All conditions in a rule are evaluated with AND logic. If any rule passes, the disposition is recommended (OR logic across rules).

RULE_CONDITION: Defines individual criteria (EQUALS, IN, NOT_EQUALS, or custom operators like CROSS_BORDER_MATCH).

Schema Definition (DDL)
SQL
-- 1. Disposition Master Table
CREATE TABLE RULE_DISPOSITION (
    DISPOSITION_ID NUMBER GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    DISPOSITION_NAME VARCHAR2(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    DESCRIPTION VARCHAR2(255),
    IS_ACTIVE NUMBER(1) DEFAULT 1 NOT NULL,
    CREATED_AT TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 2. Business Rules Table
CREATE TABLE BUSINESS_RULE (
    RULE_ID NUMBER GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    DISPOSITION_ID NUMBER NOT NULL,
    RULE_NAME VARCHAR2(100) NOT NULL,
    PRIORITY NUMBER DEFAULT 1 NOT NULL,
    IS_ACTIVE NUMBER(1) DEFAULT 1 NOT NULL,
    CONSTRAINT FK_RULE_DISP FOREIGN KEY (DISPOSITION_ID) REFERENCES RULE_DISPOSITION(DISPOSITION_ID)
);

-- 3. Atomic Rule Conditions
CREATE TABLE RULE_CONDITION (
    CONDITION_ID NUMBER GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    RULE_ID NUMBER NOT NULL,
    QUESTION_ID VARCHAR2(50) NOT NULL,
    OPERATOR VARCHAR2(30) NOT NULL, -- EQUALS, NOT_EQUALS, IN, CONTAINS_ONLY, CROSS_BORDER_MATCH
    EXPECTED_VALUE VARCHAR2(4000) NOT NULL, -- Pipe-separated values for lists (e.g. "US|UK")
    CONSTRAINT FK_COND_RULE FOREIGN KEY (RULE_ID) REFERENCES BUSINESS_RULE(RULE_ID)
);

CREATE INDEX IDX_COND_RULE_ID ON RULE_CONDITION(RULE_ID);
CREATE INDEX IDX_RULE_DISP_ID ON BUSINESS_RULE(DISPOSITION_ID);
